# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions (UBSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...; Tests/sanitize.sh sets it).
# Zamin's own targets build with -fno-sanitize-recover=all: their reports are always fatal and cannot be
# suppressed here. Only the vendor libraries' (recoverable) reports can - list each with the reason.
# Format: <check>:<function, file or library>, e.g. alignment:box2d/src/...

# miniaudio 0.11.21 (compiled in Zamin/src/Zamin/Audio/MiniaudioImpl.cpp, recoverable like a vendor library):
# its MurmurHash3 (ma_hash_32, hashing a sound's file name in the resource manager) walks the blocks with a
# negative index, ma_offset_ptr(blocks, i * sizeof(block)): the negative int becomes a huge size_t and the pointer
# addition wraps around - pointer-overflow by the letter of the standard, the right address in practice. Found by
# Clang's UBSan (GCC's does not instrument this form); the engine itself does no such arithmetic.
pointer-overflow:miniaudio.h
